core/ includes only the C++ standard library and other core/ files, never a
simulator header, so it can be used on its own: in another simulator, a routing
daemon, firmware or a closed product. Outside core/, only tools/ shares this
dual licence; the rest of the repository (the ns-3 module's model/, helper/,
test/, examples/, docs) is GPL-2.0-only. See LICENSING.md.

Much of core/ is derived from AntHocNet's dual-licensed algorithm core
(swarm-routing/AntHocNet core/, MIT OR GPL-2.0-only, its ADR-0028); each file
names its source in its header.

